          "background": "dark",
          "anchorId": "junkyard-dawgs",
          "heading": "Junkyard Dawgs",
          "body": "The Junkyard Dawgs are the immortal iron of the highway, a clan of rust-covered relics that refuse to go gently into that good scrap heap. While other drivers worry about \"factory recalls\" or \"safety ratings,\" the Dawgs rely on backwoods engineering and a \"she's good\" philosophy that defies the laws of physics and local emissions standards. To them, a check engine light isn't a warning; it’s just a complimentary interior nightlight.\n\nThe Junkyard Dawgs are the architects of automotive alchemy, keeping rust-covered relics on the road well past their prime with a stubborn refusal to acknowledge manufacturer recommendations. As part of the expanding Rush Hour Villains catalog, they represent the unpredictable threat of mechanical entropy. While they aren't actively seeking to cause chaos like more aggressive archetypes, their good enough philosophy turns every commute into a high-stakes gamble against the laws of physics and the structural integrity of 40-year-old steel.",
